      "question": {
        ":question/id": "3134fa9e-995a-5168-ba05-228c8de172f7",
        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={x}^{7}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The function $f(x)$  is the sum of two power functions. So, we apply the sum rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4/3}) \\\\  & =7{x}^{(7-1)}+\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{(4/3-1)} \\\\  & =7{x}^{6}+\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{1/3} \\\\  & =7{x}^{6}+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt[3]{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "8025cf2d-551f-5f1b-91ce-55fde811b3d0",
            ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "7883b781-a9e5-5224-8db9-e6934151bfd0",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "7{x}^{6}+\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{1/3}"
              }
            ],
